dashboard.definition:
{
	"title": "Cisco Spaces — Intelligence",
	"description": "[2026-04-25 18:10] Advanced Cisco Spaces analytics — environmental trends, ML predictions, room utilization, activation readiness, and visitor intelligence.",
	"inputs": {
		"input_global_trp": {
			"options": {
				"defaultValue": "-7d@h,now",
				"token": "global_time"
			},
			"title": "",
			"type": "input.timerange"
		}
	},
	"defaults": {
		"dataSources": {}
	},
	"visualizations": {
		"viz_about_body": {
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
				"fontColor": "#000000",
				"fontSize": "small",
				"markdown": "## About this dashboard\n\n**Cisco Spaces — Intelligence** answers six questions the customer cares about during and around an emergency-management exercise (Op Florida Ready):\n\n1. **Are the buildings comfortable?** (Environmental Intelligence)\n2. **Are we close to capacity?** (Capacity & Prediction)\n3. **Which rooms get used and which are wasted?** (Room Utilization)\n4. **Did the network handle the surge?** (Activation Readiness)\n5. **Who actually showed up — staff vs guests, repeats vs first-timers?** (Visitor Intelligence)\n6. **Did the wireless network's user experience hold up?** (Network Impact)\n\nThe dashboard cross-correlates **Cisco Spaces firehose** (people-count and presence telemetry from APs), **Cisco Catalyst Center / DNAC** (network-side health) and **Webex device telemetry** (in-room temperature & humidity sensors) to tell one coherent story.\n\n---\n\n## Data sources\n\n- **Cisco Spaces firehose — DEVICE_COUNT** (`cisco:spaces:firehose` `eventType=\"DEVICE_COUNT\"`) — `deviceCounts.userCount`, `associatedCount`, `deviceCount`, `estimatedCapacityPercentage`, location hierarchy. Filtered to floor scope (`inferredLocationTypes=FLOOR`) for per-floor panels, BUILDING scope for the campus map.\n- **Cisco Spaces firehose — DEVICE_ASSOCIATION** (`cisco:spaces:firehose` `eventType=\"DEVICE_ASSOCIATION\" event=\"ASSOCIATE\"`) — `device.macAddress`, `ssid`. Powers unique-visitor / repeat-visitor / SSID composition.\n- **Cisco Spaces firehose — DEVICE_PRESENCE** (`cisco:spaces:firehose` `eventType=\"DEVICE_PRESENCE\"`) — `macAddress`, `location.inferredLocationTypes`. Used for inter-campus traveler analysis (Sankey).\n- **Cisco Spaces firehose — SPACE_OCCUPANCY** (`cisco:spaces:firehose` `eventType=\"SPACE_OCCUPANCY\"`) — `space.name`, `space.capacity`, `peakPeopleCount`, `peoplePresence`. Used by the Room Utilization tab.\n- **Cisco Spaces firehose — WEBEX_TELEMETRY** (`cisco:spaces:firehose` `eventType=\"WEBEX_TELEMETRY\"`) — `ambientTemp`, `relativeHumidity`, `deviceInfo.serialNumber`.\n- **Cisco Catalyst Center — networkhealth** (`cisco:dnac:networkhealth`) — overall network health score (0-100) per category.\n- **Cisco Catalyst Center — clienthealth** (`cisco:dnac:clienthealth`) — overall client health score (0-100) by client type.\n- **Cisco Catalyst Center — client** (`cisco:dnac:client`) — per-client health, RSSI, SSID, band, onboarding time, site hierarchy.\n- **Cisco Catalyst Center — devicehealth** (`cisco:dnac:devicehealth`) — per-AP health, CPU/memory utilization, issue count, reachability, manageability.\n- **Cisco Catalyst Center — issue** (`cisco:dnac:issue`) — active DNAC issues with priority + site.\n- **Cisco Catalyst Center — compliance** (`cisco:dnac:compliance`) — per-device compliance status.\n\n---\n\n## Tab 1 — Environmental Intelligence\n\n- **Avg temperature / Avg humidity** — mean across all Webex room sensors over the selected time range. Temperature converted Celsius → Fahrenheit via `temp_f = round(temp*9/5+32, 2)`.\n- **Current sensor readings** — latest temp + humidity per Webex device, with a comfort verdict: `Optimal` if 68-76 °F and 30-60 % RH; otherwise `Warm/Humid` or `Cool/Dry`.\n- **Temperature / Humidity by floor + exercise annotations** — hourly average per device, with vertical markers for the three Op Florida Ready dates pulled from the shared `ds_annotations` saved search.\n- **Spaces × Webex — occupancy + temperature overlay** — hourly occupancy (`deviceCounts.userCount`) as columns, hourly temperature as overlay line. Visual answer to \"do crowds heat the room?\"\n- **Spaces × Webex — people vs. temperature scatter** — one dot per hour. Upward slope = thermal-load correlation.\n\n---\n\n## Tab 2 — Capacity & Prediction\n\n- **Peak users today** — max value of `max(users) by _time, floor` in the period (busiest hour on busiest floor).\n- **Avg users (period)** — mean of those hourly per-floor maxima — your \"typical concurrent population\" baseline.\n- **Highest / Second-highest capacity floor (period peak)** — per-floor max of `deviceCounts.estimatedCapacityPercentage` over the window, scoped to the two specific buildings.\n- **Users by city over time** — hourly peak `userCount` summed across all floors of a city.\n- **Occupancy forecast (24-hour prediction)** — Splunk `predict` on the hourly user-count series, projecting 24 h forward with 95 % confidence band.\n- **Capacity % by floor over time** — hourly max `estimatedCapacityPercentage` per floor; `useother=t` keeps the top 10 floors visible.\n- **This week vs last week** — hourly user count split by `if(_time >= now()-7d, \"This Week\", \"Last Week\")`.\n\n---\n\n## Tab 3 — Room Utilization\n\nSource: `cisco:spaces:firehose eventType=SPACE_OCCUPANCY`. Each event reports a room, its capacity, peak headcount, and a presence flag.\n\n- **Total rooms** — `dc(spaceOccupancy.space.name)` (distinct rooms reporting any data).\n- **Ghost rooms** — ROOM spaces where `peoplePresence!=\"true\" AND peakPeopleCount==0` for ≥ 80 % of observations in the window. Effectively never used.\n- **Hot rooms** — ROOM spaces where `avg(peakPeopleCount) / capacity ≥ 0.5`. These rooms are consistently above half capacity.\n- **Rooms by utilization tier (pie)** — tiers from `avg(peakPeopleCount)/capacity`: Hot (≥ 80 %), Active (40-80 %), Idle (< 40 %), Empty (≈ 0).\n- **Top 15 rooms by utilization** — bar chart sorted by `avg(peakPeopleCount)/capacity * 100`.\n- **Room utilization detail** — full table: building, floor, room, capacity, avg/peak utilization %, time-occupied %, report count.\n\n---\n\n## Tab 4 — Activation Readiness\n\nTells the \"did the network survive Op Florida Ready\" story. The activation window is configurable via the time-range input.\n\n- **Peak users / Peak capacity % / Peak temperature** — max within the activation window across each metric.\n- **WiFi associations** — total `count` of `eventType=\"DEVICE_ASSOCIATION\" event=\"ASSOCIATE\"` events.\n- **Spaces — occupancy surge + Op Florida Ready annotations** — hourly total occupancy (area chart) with the three exercise dates marked.\n- **Webex — temperature & humidity during activation** — avg temp + humidity on the same hourly axis.\n- **Spaces — WiFi associations by SSID + exercise annotations** — hourly assoc count stacked by SSID, top 10.\n- **Surge multiplier (single value)** — `avg(people) during exercise window / avg(people) during prior baseline week`. ≥ 2.0 means the activation roughly doubled the on-site population.\n- **Same metrics, side-by-side** — bar comparing baseline vs exercise for people / unique users / unique devices.\n\n> **Why some windows are dynamic**: panels that compare \"exercise vs baseline\" use `strptime` hardcoded windows (`2026-04-13` → `2026-04-16` exercise, `2026-04-06` → `2026-04-13` baseline) so they remain stable regardless of the dashboard's time-range input. Panels that visualize \"during the activation\" use the dashboard's time-range input so analysts can probe different sub-windows.\n\n---\n\n## Tab 5 — Visitor Intelligence\n\nSource: `cisco:spaces:firehose eventType=DEVICE_ASSOCIATION` + `DEVICE_PRESENCE`.\n\n- **Unique devices** — `dc(deviceAssociation.device.macAddress)` over the window.\n- **Repeat visitors %** — `(devices seen on ≥ 2 distinct days) / total devices * 100`.\n- **Inter-campus travelers** — devices whose `devicePresence` events include more than one BUILDING. Used as the Sankey input.\n- **Guest vs employee (pie)** — SSID-based: any SSID matching `(?i)guest` is Guest; everything else is Employee.\n- **Daily visitors with 7-day forecast** — `predict` on the daily unique-device count; projects 7 days forward.\n- **Guest vs employee by day** — same SSID classification, daily association counts.\n- **Dwell time distribution** — per-MAC, per-day association window: `latest(_time) - earliest(_time)`. Bucketed 0-15 m / 15 m-1 h / 1-4 h / 4 h+.\n\n---\n\n## Tab 6 — Network Impact\n\nPulls in DNAC alongside Spaces so a single timeline shows what the network was doing while people were on it.\n\n- **Network health / Client health (single value, 0-100)** — DNAC `cisco:dnac:networkhealth` `category=\"All\"` and `cisco:dnac:clienthealth` `clientType=\"ALL\" scoreType=\"ALL\"`, hourly latest, 2-decimal rounded.\n- **Active DNAC issues** — `dc(IssueID)` from `cisco:dnac:issue`.\n- **Compliance rate** — `count(eval(ComplianceStatus=\"COMPLIANT\"))/count` of `cisco:dnac:compliance`.\n- **Spaces × DNAC — occupancy + DNAC issues** — hourly occupancy column chart; high-severity DNAC issues drawn as overlay markers; exercise dates annotated.\n- **DNAC × DNAC — network & client health + DNAC issues** — both health series + issue overlay on one timeline.\n- **Spaces × DNAC — occupancy vs. client-health scatter** — one dot per hour. Negative slope = \"more people, worse network.\"\n- **Spaces × DNAC — occupancy + RSSI overlay** — hourly assoc count (column) + avg `connection.rssi` (line). Does signal degrade with crowd?\n- **Client health by site over time** — `health.overallScore` per site, per hour.\n- **Spaces × DNAC — occupancy + onboarding-time overlay** — hourly assoc count + avg onboarding-time.\n- **DNAC issues by severity stacked + occupancy overlay** — stacked-bar of issue severity (HIGH/MED/LOW) with occupancy line.\n- **AP health distribution (pie)** — APs grouped by `latest(OverallHealth)`: Excellent (9-10) / Good (7-8) / Fair (5-6) / Poor (0-4).\n- **Client radio band split** — `connection.band` distribution (2.4 vs 5 GHz).\n- **DNAC issues by site** — `dc(IssueID)` per `SiteName`.\n- **AP detail table** — per-AP latest health, CPU %, mem %, issue count, client counts per band, air quality.\n\n---\n\n## Color coding (table cells)\n\nA subset of tables across the dashboard suite uses cell-background tints to highlight what needs attention. Palette is dark-mode-safe (rgba):\n\n- 🔴 **Critical** `rgba(214,69,80,0.35)` — needs attention now (Unreachable, Unmanaged, NON_COMPLIANT, P1, Critical CPU/memory).\n- 🟠 **Warning** `rgba(229,168,35,0.30)` — watch (Managed With Errors, P2, Warning CPU/memory, At-Risk site).\n- 🟢 **Healthy** `rgba(110,190,74,0.15)` — subtle green tint (Reachable, Managed, P3/P4, OK).\n\nCurrently colored on **this** dashboard: none — Spaces tables are mostly numeric ranges. We can add tier coloring to AP detail and Room utilization tables in a follow-up if useful.\n\n---\n\n## Architecture\n\nAll active panels now use inline `ds.search` data sources. Earlier versions chained many panels from raw hidden base searches, but Dashboard Studio can render those post-process chains inconsistently even when the same SPL works in Search. Keeping each panel self-contained makes dashboard results match Open in Search and keeps time-token handling explicit.\n\n---\n\n## Known caveats\n\n1. **Field extraction multivalues**: `healthScore` and `scoreValue` from `cisco:dnac:networkhealth` / `cisco:dnac:clienthealth` arrive as multivalue arrays (e.g., `['99','99']`) due to JSON path duplication during indexing. The Network Impact KPIs collapse this with `bin _time | stats latest(field) by _time` rather than `timechart latest(eval(round(...)))` (which silently returns null on multivalues).\n2. **Forecast accuracy**: `predict` panels (capacity 24 h, daily visitors 7 d) need at least ~3 weeks of data for stable projections. With less, the confidence bands will look very wide.\n3. **Op Florida Ready windows are hardcoded** in the activation comparison panels (`2026-04-13` → `2026-04-16` exercise, baseline = preceding week). Update the `strptime` calls if the exercise dates shift.\n4. **No Meraki, no SD-WAN data in this environment**. Any panel referencing those would be empty by definition; they've been removed across the dashboard suite."
			},
			"type": "splunk.markdown"
		},
		"viz_about_hdr": {
			"options": {
				"fontColor": "#049FD9",
				"fontSize": "small",
				"markdown": "## About — Metrics Reference"
			},
			"type": "splunk.markdown"
		},
		"viz_act_box": {
			"options": {
				"fillColor": "#FFFFFF",
				"strokeColor": "#E0E0E0"
			},
			"type": "splunk.rectangle"
		},
		"viz_act_compare_chart": {
			"dataSources": {
				"primary": "ds_act_compare_chart"
			},
			"description": "People / unique users / unique devices: first half vs second half of the selected time range.",
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "transparent",
				"legendDisplay": "bottom",
				"seriesColors": [
					"#9E9E9E",
					"#D64550"
				],
				"xAxisTitleVisibility": "hide",
				"yAxisTitleText": "Avg per hour"
			},
			"title": "Spaces baseline × exercise — same metrics, side-by-side",
			"type": "splunk.column"
		},
		"viz_act_compare_kpi": {
			"dataSources": {
				"primary": "ds_act_compare_kpi"
			},
			"description": "Surge multiplier — second half vs first half of the selected time range.",
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "transparent",
				"majorColor": "> primary | seriesByName('multiplier') | lastPoint() | rangeValue(thresholds=[1.5, 3], colors=[\"#9E9E9E\", \"#FF8C25\", \"#D64550\"])",
				"shouldAbbreviateMajorValue": true,
				"shouldAbbreviateTrendValue": true,
				"unit": "x",
				"unitPosition": "after"
			},
			"title": "Spaces baseline × exercise — surge multiplier",
			"type": "splunk.singlevalue"
		},
		"viz_act_env": {
			"dataSources": {
				"primary": "ds_activation_env"
			},
			"description": "Avg temp & humidity over the activation period.",
			"options": {
				"nullValueDisplay": "connect",
				"seriesColors": [
					"#D64550",
					"#049FD9"
				]
			},
			"title": "Webex — temperature & humidity during activation",
			"type": "splunk.line"
		},
		"viz_act_hdr": {
			"options": {
				"fontColor": "#D64550",
				"markdown": "**Activation Readiness**"
			},
			"type": "splunk.markdown"
		},
		"viz_act_kpi_capacity": {
			"dataSources": {
				"primary": "ds_activation_kpi_capacity"
			},
			"description": "Peak building capacity-percent during the activation.",
			"options": {
				"majorColor": "#FF8C25",
				"shouldAbbreviateMajorValue": true,
				"shouldAbbreviateTrendValue": true
			},
			"title": "Peak capacity %",
			"type": "splunk.singlevalue"
		},
		"viz_act_kpi_peak": {
			"dataSources": {
				"primary": "ds_activation_kpi_peak"
			},
			"description": "Peak users during a known exercise.",
			"options": {
				"majorColor": "#049FD9",
				"shouldAbbreviateMajorValue": true,
				"shouldAbbreviateTrendValue": true
			},
			"title": "Peak users",
			"type": "splunk.singlevalue"
		},
		"viz_act_kpi_ssid": {
			"dataSources": {
				"primary": "ds_activation_kpi_ssid"
			},
			"description": "Total wireless associations during the activation.",
			"options": {
				"majorColor": "#6EBE4A",
				"shouldAbbreviateMajorValue": true,
				"shouldAbbreviateTrendValue": true
			},
			"title": "WiFi associations",
			"type": "splunk.singlevalue"
		},
		"viz_act_kpi_temp": {
			"dataSources": {
				"primary": "ds_activation_kpi_temp"
			},
			"description": "Peak temperature during the activation.",
			"options": {
				"majorColor": "#D64550",
				"shouldAbbreviateMajorValue": true,
				"shouldAbbreviateTrendValue": true,
				"unit": "°F"
			},
			"title": "Peak temperature",
			"type": "splunk.singlevalue"
		},
		"viz_act_surge": {
			"dataSources": {
				"annotation": "ds_activation_annotation",
				"primary": "ds_activation_surge"
			},
			"description": "Hour-by-hour total occupancy during the selected window. Red markers show exact dates/times of known exercises (e.g., Operation Florida Ready). Lets you see surges line up with declared activations.",
			"options": {
				"annotationColor": [
					"#D64550"
				],
				"annotationLabel": [
					"label"
				],
				"nullValueDisplay": "connect",
				"seriesColors": [
					"#049FD9"
				]
			},
			"title": "Spaces — occupancy surge + Op Florida Ready annotations",
			"type": "splunk.area"
		},
		"viz_act_wifi": {
			"dataSources": {
				"annotation": "ds_activation_annotation",
				"primary": "ds_activation_wifi"
			},
			"description": "Hourly WiFi associations stacked by SSID + exercise overlays.",
			"options": {
				"annotationColor": [
					"#D64550"
				],
				"annotationLabel": [
					"label"
				],
				"seriesColors": [
					"#049FD9",
					"#6EBE4A",
					"#7B56DB",
					"#FF8C25"
				],
				"stackMode": "stacked"
			},
			"title": "Spaces — WiFi associations by SSID + exercise annotations",
			"type": "splunk.column"
		},
		"viz_ap_health_dist": {
			"dataSources": {
				"primary": "ds_ap_health_dist"
			},
			"description": "Access points grouped by health tier (Excellent → Poor).",
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "transparent",
				"seriesColors": [
					"#00cdaf",
					"#009ceb",
					"#dd9900",
					"#ff677b",
					"#a0a0a0"
				],
				"showDonutHole": true
			},
			"showLastUpdated": false,
			"showProgressBar": false,
			"title": "DNAC — access-point health distribution",
			"type": "splunk.pie"
		},
		"viz_ap_health_table": {
			"dataSources": {
				"primary": "ds_ap_health_table"
			},
			"description": "Detailed table for every access point: site, health score, CPU and memory utilization, open issues, client counts on each band, and air-quality / interference scores. The operational worksheet for the wireless team.",
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "transparent",
				"fontSize": "small"
			},
			"showLastUpdated": false,
			"showProgressBar": false,
			"title": "DNAC — access-point detail",
			"type": "splunk.table"
		},
		"viz_band_distribution": {
			"dataSources": {
				"primary": "ds_band_distribution"
			},
			"description": "Wireless clients split by band (2.4 vs 5 GHz).",
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "transparent",
				"seriesColors": [
					"#009ceb",
					"#7b56db",
					"#00cdaf"
				],
				"showDonutHole": true
			},
			"showLastUpdated": false,
			"showProgressBar": false,
			"title": "DNAC — client radio band split (2.4 vs. 5 GHz)",
			"type": "splunk.pie"
		},
		"viz_cap_box": {
			"options": {
				"fillColor": "#FFFFFF",
				"strokeColor": "#E0E0E0"
			},
			"type": "splunk.rectangle"
		},
		"viz_cap_gauge_first": {
			"dataSources": {
				"primary": "ds_capacity_gauge_first"
			},
			"description": "Peak utilization of the busiest floor.",
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "transparent",
				"majorColor": "> primary | seriesByName('Capacity %') | lastPoint() | rangeValue(thresholds=[50, 80], colors=[\"#6EBE4A\", \"#FF8C25\", \"#D64550\"])",
				"shouldAbbreviateMajorValue": true,
				"shouldAbbreviateTrendValue": true,
				"unit": "%",
				"unitPosition": "after"
			},
			"title": "Highest capacity floor (period peak)",
			"type": "splunk.singlevalue"
		},
		"viz_cap_gauge_second": {
			"dataSources": {
				"primary": "ds_capacity_gauge_second"
			},
			"description": "Second-busiest floor — the next pressure point you'd address.",
			"options": {
				"backgroundColor": "transparent",
				"majorColor": "> primary | seriesByName('Capacity %') | lastPoint() | rangeValue(thresholds=[50, 80], colors=[\"#6EBE4A\", \"#FF8C25\", \"#D64550\"])",
				"shouldAbbreviateMajorValue": true,
				"shouldAbbreviateTrendValue": true,
				"unit": "%",
				"unitPosition": "after"
			},
			"title": "Second highest capacity floor (period peak)",
			"type": "splunk.singlevalue"
		},
		"viz_cap_hdr": {
			"options": {
				"fontColor": "#D64550",
				"markdown": "**Capacity and Prediction**"
			},
			"type": "splunk.markdown"
		},
		"viz_cap_trend": {
			"dataSources": {
				"annotation": "ds_activation_annotation",
				"primary": "ds_capacity_trend"
			},
			"description": "Estimated capacity percentage from Cisco Spaces",
			"options": {
				"annotationColor": [
					"#D64550"
				],
				"annotationLabel": [
					"label"
				],
				"nullValueDisplay": "connect",
				"seriesColors": [
					"#049FD9",
					"#6EBE4A",
					"#7B56DB"
				]
			},
			"title": "Capacity % by floor over time",
			"type": "splunk.line"
		},
		"viz_capacity_predict": {
			"dataSources": {
				"annotation": "ds_activation_annotation",
				"primary": "ds_capacity_predict"
			},
			"description": "ML predict command projects total users 24 hours forward",
			"options": {
				"annotationColor": [
					"#D64550"
				],
				"annotationLabel": [
					"label"
				],
				"nullValueDisplay": "connect",
				"seriesColors": [
					"#049FD9",
					"#D64550",
					"#CCCCCC",
					"#CCCCCC"
				]
			},
			"title": "Occupancy forecast (24-hour prediction)",
			"type": "splunk.line"
		},
		"viz_client_health_by_site": {
			"dataSources": {
				"annotation": "ds_activation_annotation",
				"primary": "ds_client_health_by_site"
			},
			"description": "Hourly client-health score broken out per site.",
			"options": {
				"annotationColor": [
					"#D64550"
				],
				"annotationLabel": [
					"label"
				],
				"backgroundColor": "transparent",
				"legendDisplay": "bottom",
				"nullValueDisplay": "connect",
				"seriesColors": [
					"#009ceb",
					"#00cdaf",
					"#7b56db",
					"#dd9900",
					"#ff677b",
					"#cb2196",
					"#813193",
					"#0051b5"
				],
				"xAxisTitleVisibility": "hide",
				"yAxisTitleText": "Client Health (0-10)"
			},
			"showLastUpdated": false,
			"showProgressBar": false,
			"title": "DNAC — client health by site over time",
			"type": "splunk.line"
		},
		"viz_convergence_health": {
			"dataSources": {
				"annotation": "ds_convergence_annotations",
				"primary": "ds_convergence_health"
			},
			"description": "DNAC network & client health on the same hourly timeline as issues.",
			"options": {
				"annotationColor": [
					"#D64550"
				],
				"annotationLabel": [
					"label"
				],
				"legendDisplay": "bottom",
				"markerDisplay": "filled",
				"nullValueDisplay": "connect",
				"seriesColors": [
					"#6EBE4A",
					"#7B56DB"
				],
				"xAxisTitleVisibility": "hide",
				"yAxisTitleText": "Health Score (0-100)"
			},
			"title": "DNAC × DNAC — network & client health + DNAC issues + date annotations",
			"type": "splunk.line"
		},
		"viz_convergence_occupancy": {
			"dataSources": {
				"annotation": "ds_convergence_annotations",
				"primary": "ds_convergence_occupancy"
			},
			"description": "Hourly Spaces occupancy with high-severity DNAC issues marked.",
			"options": {
				"annotationColor": [
					"#D64550"
				],
				"annotationLabel": [
					"label"
				],
				"legendDisplay": "off",
				"seriesColors": [
					"#049FD9"
				],
				"xAxisTitleVisibility": "hide",
				"yAxisTitleText": "Occupancy (people)"
			},
			"title": "Spaces × DNAC — occupancy + DNAC issues + date annotations",
			"type": "splunk.column"
		},
		"viz_dwell_bar": {
			"dataSources": {
